  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">URBAN:  Urban Resilience Building and Nature: Innovating Urban Planning for Resiliency with Nature-based Solutions and Climate Risk Models in Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thailand has been identified as one of the most vulnerable countries in the world to climate change. The project improves the social, economic and environmental resilience of urban areas and the landscapes in which they are embedded to the impacts of climate change by introducing nature-based solutions (NbS). It makes a significant contribution to climate change adaptation in up to six pilot sites in two Thai provinces. Adaptation is enhanced through a variety of potential NbS measures, including wetland restoration, conservation and management, enhanced management of the urban environment, forest and mangrove restoration, the creation of urban protected areas and green spaces, and sustainable land use plans. The aim is to develop cost-effective, replicable models that can be scaled and transferred to other areas in Thailand.</narrative>
  </description>
